<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 21 August, from 1331 to 2017.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1331">1331 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">695 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stefan Dušan captures his father Stefan Dečanski at Petrič</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the Serbian civil war, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a> took Petrič after a siege and imprisoned his father, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-decanski">Stefan Uroš III Dečanski</a>, in Zvečan Fortress, where he died in November. Dušan became King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> in September.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-decanski">Stefan Dečanski</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1415">1415 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">611 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Portugal captures Ceuta from the Marinid Sultanate</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Portuguese forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> I, among them his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Prince Henry the Navigator</a>, took the North African port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a> from the Marinid Sultanate after a carefully prepared attack. The capture marked the beginning of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conquest-of-ceuta">Conquest of Ceuta</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Prince Henry the Navigator</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1680">1680 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">346 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Spanish colonists abandon Santa Fe during the Pueblo Revolt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Besieged by Pueblo fighters led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope">Popé</a>, the Spanish governor and settlers retreated from Santa Fe towards El Paso. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pueblo-peoples">Pueblo peoples</a> kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a> free of Spanish rule for twelve years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1689">1689 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">337 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cameronians repel the Jacobites at Dunkeld</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A small regiment of Cameronians held the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunkeld">Dunkeld</a> against a much larger Jacobite force. The defeat broke the momentum of the rising that had followed Killiecrankie.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1716">1716 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">310 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Ottomans abandon the siege of Corfu</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">News of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-petrovaradin">Battle of Petrovaradin</a> and the arrival of naval reinforcements forced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> to abandon their siege of Corfu, held by the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. It was Venice's last major military success and preserved its rule over the Ionian Islands.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-petrovaradin">Battle of Petrovaradin</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1858">1858 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">168 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln and Douglas hold their first debate</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a> and Senator Stephen Douglas met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottawa">Ottawa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a>, for the first of seven debates on the spread of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. Lincoln lost the Senate race but won national attention.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1911">1911 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">115 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Mona Lisa is stolen from the Louvre</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Italian handyman Vincenzo Peruggia walked out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louvre">Louvre</a> with the Mona Lisa under his smock. The theft made the painting world-famous; it was recovered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> in 1913.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louvre">Louvre</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1959">1959 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">67 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hawaii becomes the 50th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a> proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>'s admission as the 50th state. It was the first state outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> and the first with an Asian American plurality.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2017">2017 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">9 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Total solar eclipse crosses the United States coast to coast</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a>'s shadow swept from Oregon to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a>, the first total eclipse to cross the whole country since 1918. Tens of millions watched along the path of totality.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
